WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.330
The street signs for the new US embassy have already gone up.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:08.000
This usually quiet, residential neighborhood in south Jerusalem

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.160
has become the focus of the world's attention.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:16.000
"The building behind me, which currently houses
the consular services of the US,

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.599
will become the new American Embassy.

00:00:19.599 --> 00:00:24.340
Moving the embassy from Tel Aviv to Jerusalem is highly controversial.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.000
The international consensus remains that the status of the city

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.800
should be agreed upon through negotiations."

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:38.000
For now, only the US ambassador and a limited number of staff offices will move to Jerusalem from Tel Aviv.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.510
The complete relocation will take many years.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:46.500
A majority of Israelis supports the US move
– like here in downtown West Jerusalem.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:52.200
"Jerusalem is, after all, the capital of Israel; I believe it, and of course there will be,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.970
I believe there should be someday a Palestinian state.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:59.200
and if they want part of Jerusalem, someday they’ll
find an agreement.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:05.000
But I think it’s OK the US does move the
embassy over here, because this is after all the capital.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.439
In Israel, ask every kid what’s our capital: It's Jerusalem."

00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:15.350
"I think the American Embassy should be in
Jerusalem.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:20.530
I think all the embassies, including the US
embassy of course, should be in Jerusalem,

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:23.979
because Jerusalem is the capital of Israel."

00:01:23.979 --> 00:01:30.880
Observers say that the de facto recognition
by the US will have long-term consequences:

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.080
"Jerusalem today is more divided,
more binational, less sustainable

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.600
and more contested than ever before.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.039
And nothing has changed about that.

00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:43.340
This move is a hollow gesture.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:49.840
On the other hand, it indicates a collapse
of the United States stewardship over political processes

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.820
and tells the Palestinians and the
Arab world,

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.920
'Abandon hope, you are about to lose Jerusalem.'"

00:01:56.929 --> 00:02:02.420
On the other side of town, in East Jerusalem,
Palestinians are following the move closely.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:07.619
They want this part of the city to be their
capital in a future independent state.

00:02:07.619 --> 00:02:12.530
Many here say that the US President is giving
away something that is not his to give.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:16.890
"If they move the US embassy, whatever
they do, Palestine will remain Arab.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:22.500
We will defend this land,
we are present, and it's our greatest right to live in this land."

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.260
"Moving the embassy to Jerusalem shows only one thing:

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.280
It shows completely that the Americans are on the side of the Israelis.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.020
They do not care about Palestinian rights."

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:39.800
"For many 
Palestinians, the US has long lost its role as an honest broker in any peace initiative.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.820
And while the Palestinians' dream of statehood fades,

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:48.300
Israel is hoping that more countries will follow
the US's lead and move their embassies to Jerusalem."

